# INVWINDE.KEY - a key script of INVWIN, as INVWIN.KEY, run with the
# [intl] of TEST/WIN/INTLDE.INI (INVWIN_WININTLDE): short dates d.M.yyyy,
# a decimal comma, a thousands point, no 0 before the comma; on the data
# of TEST/KEYS/SEED.REQ and INTLDE.REQ (INVWIN_WINSEEDDE), which adds item
# 1001 of 1234 units, 1200 of them lent, and a reservation ended.  Item
# 2's form in edit mode shows its read-only dates in that form, its ID
# and editable fields as they are (ITEMEDIT); ESC leaves it.  Item 1's
# service records show their dates so (RECORDS).  INS adds a record, its
# date typed as ISO and its cost 12345.67, which the list shows grouped
# (ADDED); in view mode its date and cost show so, the record numbers as
# they are (SHOWN); in edit mode the date and the cost are as typed
# (EDIT).  ESC twice goes back to the item list; Items > Service lists
# both records, the new one first (RECENT).  ESC and END select item
# 1001, its ID as it is, its quantity grouped (ITEMEND), and ENTER shows
# it in view mode, its numbers and dates so (ITEMVIEW).  Items > Loans
# and holds shows the open loan (LOANS), five CTRL+PGDNs every row, the ended
# reservation too (LOANALL); Admin > Users shows the users' last logins
# (USERS) and the audit log of item 1001 its dates (AUDIT), its record
# and values as they are.  The end by Exit.  No snapshot holds the day
# of the run.  TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/INVWINDE.SNP is its snapshot.
T ADMIN
K TAB
T Retro1986
K ENTER DOWN CTRL-E
S ITEMEDIT
K ESC UP ALT-C S
S RECORDS
K INS
T 2026-10-05
# DOWN picks the first type, TAB goes on to the summary, then the cost
K TAB DOWN TAB
T Cleaned the drive heads
K TAB
T 12345.67
K ENTER
S ADDED
K DOWN ENTER
S SHOWN
K ENTER CTRL-E
S EDIT
K ESC ESC ALT-I E
S RECENT
K ESC END
S ITEMEND
K ENTER
S ITEMVIEW
K ESC ALT-I O
S LOANS
K CPGDN CPGDN CPGDN CPGDN CPGDN
S LOANALL
K ALT-A U
S USERS
K ALT-A A TAB
T 1001
K ENTER
T items
K ENTER
S AUDIT
K ESC ALT-F X
